WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love this show so much.
-Thank you, Seth.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.569 line:92%
-You've been here in past years,

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.171
talking about your great show
"Detroiters," which I also love.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
It has been so fun.
We met as writers at "SNL,"

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
and to watch you
doing sketch comedy like this

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.145 size:75% position:38% line:92%
makes me very happy.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.813
You're doing it with Zach Kanin.
-That's right.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.216
-John Solomon, both writers
you met at "SNL" as well.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:19.486
What was your -- was it fun
to sit in the room and write?

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.220 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And do you feel like

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've gotten better at
writing sketches,

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as the speed
in which you write them?

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm...No, not really.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like we still --
Coming from "SNL,"

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we still have
that same work mentality,

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is, like,
you sit around --

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get there early,
but then you just sit there

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.337 size:78% position:39%
and [Bleep] and talk,
and then you're like,

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my God!
We got to do something!"

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.075
-So it's still that same thing.
-Right.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We need that ticking clock,
I think.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:47.580
-You have some great guest stars
from your time there as well --

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.249 line:92%
Vanessa Bayer, Cecily Strong,

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.351 line:92%
our friend Conner O'Malley...

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:55.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
Will Forte --
one of my favorite sketches.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel like Will --
You used him

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.127 line:92%
as well you could ever use him.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:01.928 line:92%
It was an airplane sketch.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's what Will's
looking like.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, um --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:10.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, do you want to give up
the premise of this sketch?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:10.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:15.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so he --
A long time ago, 30 years ago,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
took a flight, and a baby --
he was going to London,

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:22.015
and a baby cried the entire time
and ruined his flight

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then ruined his trip
to London.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:27.854
So he vowed to get revenge
on me, who was the little baby.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then, while I'm going
on my honeymoon,

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:35.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's like, "Remember me?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there's a lot of
close screaming.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:42.602
How -- like, how hard was it to
get through a sketch like that

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a two-shot with Forte
screaming at you?

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was so hard.
Akiva had -- The director.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.174 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Akiva, also from "SNL."

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.043
The Lonely Island produced
this show, I should know.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep. And he kept having him
to be like,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:55.548
"Tim, you're on camera, man.
You can't just be like..."

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.953 line:92%
Forte would come in and be like,

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I hope my breath is okay,
buddy."

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
"I think you should leave"

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
is basically the statement
of thesis for this whole show.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of the characters
are people

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
who just fully commit
to something.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that is a perfect sort
of opening sentence,

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
that sketch
that we just showed --

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
of people who will not admit
they're wrong.

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And it was fun to watch

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there are some things
that I remember

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
even you having written
at "SNL" --

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-You know,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
that for whatever reason
didn't work there

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.150 line:92%
that sort of flourish here.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:30.984 line:92%
Was that fun to find things that

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had thought were funny
maybe five years ago

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.687
and now finally have them
fully realized on camera?

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely. It was so great.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, things that didn't work
on "SNL" or like, yeah.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.760
It was so nice to be able
to bring them back and be like,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay, it is okay."
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I am okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There were so many
guest stars I recognize

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're friends with.
There was one scene

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it's basically a --
What do you call it?

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
A focus group.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:58.678
-...to talk about things people
want in a new car.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-There was an actor in it.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do want to show a clip
of him, but real quick --

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.251 size:78% position:39%
Did you just find --
How did you find him?

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.553 line:92%
-His name is Ruben Rabasa,

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he auditioned,
and we were blown away.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:13.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a very good actor.
-And I will say watching this,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.995
I thought, "Oh, my God,
you've found the perfect person

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a Tim and Zach sketch,"
'cause he's real crazy.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let's take a look
at what I'm talking about.

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do we think
it should look like?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sleek.
-Good.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
-High tech.
-Aerodynamic.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Too small.
-I'm sorry?

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Too small.
So when you get in there,

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:36.115
you're like,
"If the steering wheel fly off,

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.050 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm toast."

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. Okay, I don't know why
we'd make it too small.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:42.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it's a good idea
and I stand by.

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:45.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Maybe it could have,
like, a sporty look.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great.
-Teacher's pet.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Any other ideas?
-Stinky!

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:56.402 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:59.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just -- I don't know what
I love about him so much.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it is --
-And I just realized,

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:04.410
showing Forte and playing him,
they got a real similar look.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.815
-Not every character on the show
looks like that.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:10.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
It must be really weird

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you, as an actor
who, that's your actual look,

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:14.554 line:92%
come in and you see Forte.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:18.324
And that's what they made him to
look crazy in a sketch,

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.193
and you're just like --
-"Hey, that's what I look like."

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:24.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. "That's my, like,
normal look, man."

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've talked about your kids.
You've got one of each.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
Penny is your daughter, yeah?
-Yep.

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she shows up on
your Instagram.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.173
She's kind of an Instagram star.
-Yeah, she is.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:38.444
-Does she love the camera?
-She does. She really does.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
But last time
I came on the show, I --

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.316 size:81% position:41%
We talked about her,
and when I got home --

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:46.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, she does funny bits,
and I ask her

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I can record them,
and sometimes she says "yes,"

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:49.922 size:88% position:44% line:92%
sometimes she says "no."

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.025
But she did a funny bit, and I
was like, "Can I record that?"

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:54.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like,
"You gotta pay me money."

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.662 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:59.399
And I was like, "You know what?
You're 100% right.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I respect that."

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now if I record one.
I give her money.

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:03.536 line:92%
-Oh, wow, just on the recording?

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just -- yeah.
I'm like, "Yeah, okay."

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like, "5 bucks."
-Okay.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.740
-She'll negotiate with me, too.
-With this one,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.877
I think it was Wi-Fi hot spot.
Is that what we're gonna watch?

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.012
-We had just moved and we didn't
have Wi-Fi yet,

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
so she wanted me to set up
a Wi-Fi hotspot with my phone.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. And I think she was
pretty cool about it.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's take a look.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:23.389 line:92%
-Get me a Wi-Fi hotspot now!

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.859 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.998 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Now, I said.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:34.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:39.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-Yep, yep, yep. Penny!

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
10 bucks is coming home
for you, Penny.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:45.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What about Buster?
Buster is older? Younger?

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Buster is older.
-Gotcha.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.280 line:92%
And does Buster love the camera?

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hold on. Let me put this
in my pocket. I don't wanna...

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:53.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
He doesn't like the camera
as much.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-He's super funny, too,

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he doesn't want me
to record him, so I don't.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he, like, dances
around the house and stuff.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:01.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I also appreciate a kid
who doesn't love the camera,

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
so give that to Buster for me.
-Oh, my God.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:05.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I don't want
to just reward, you know,

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:06.766 line:92%
people who love the lens.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:09.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:11.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need some behind the camera
people as well, you know?

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.773
-Yes, people who don't want
to be in front of the camera

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
get paid, too.
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
Buddy, congratulations
on the show.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:21.647
I cannot tell everyone here
how much you have to see it.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just always such
a pleasure to have you here.

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:27.019
-Thank you, buddy.
-That's Tim Robinson, everybody.

